@api = http://localhost:4000
# Run GET /people first, then paste any id here:
@personId = fa8301e435fbdf550254dd23

### 1. People
GET {{api}}/people

### 2. A page that exists
GET {{api}}/resolve?address=tidepool.zz

### 3. Messy capitalization still finds it
GET {{api}}/resolve?address=%20TidePool.ZZ%20

### 4. An address that leads nowhere (still a normal 200 response)
GET {{api}}/resolve?address=kelp-forest.zz

### 5. Record a visit
POST {{api}}/visits
Content-Type: application/json

{ "personId": "{{personId}}", "address": "tidepool.zz", "via": "typed" }

### 6. Record a visit to nowhere
POST {{api}}/visits
Content-Type: application/json

{ "personId": "{{personId}}", "address": "kelp-forest.zz", "via": "link" }

### 7. History, 5 at a time
GET {{api}}/history?personId={{personId}}&limit=5

### 8. Search
GET {{api}}/search?q=steam

### 9. Publish a new site
POST {{api}}/sites
Content-Type: application/json

{ "authorId": "{{personId}}", "address": "mytest.zz", "title": "My Test", "html": "<h1>Hello</h1><p>My first page about <a href=\"tidepool.zz\">tides</a>.</p>" }

### 10. Publish the same address again as the same person (adds a revision)
POST {{api}}/sites
Content-Type: application/json

{ "authorId": "{{personId}}", "address": "mytest.zz", "title": "My Test v2", "html": "<p>Second version.</p>" }

### 11. Attack attempt: scripts, handlers, javascript links, images
POST {{api}}/sites
Content-Type: application/json

{ "authorId": "{{personId}}", "address": "evil.zz", "title": "Evil", "html": "<h1>Hi</h1><script>alert(1)</script><img src=x onerror=alert(1)><a href=\"javascript:alert(1)\">click</a><iframe src=\"http://evil.com\"></iframe>" }

### 12. Read the attack page back
GET {{api}}/resolve?address=evil.zz

### 13. Bad address
POST {{api}}/sites
Content-Type: application/json

{ "authorId": "{{personId}}", "address": "not an address", "title": "x", "html": "<p>x</p>" }

###
GET {{api}}/history?personId={{personId}}&limit=5&before=2026-11-05T09:33:00.000Z